# Millennium Druid

## Lore

The Millennium Druids pattern their lives after their sacred Tree of Life. They are peace loving men and women of healing and learning, dedicated to the protection of the Millennium Trees and all life, and they eat no animal of any kind. Most wander the land like gentle knights-errant, teaching, helping and healing the people and animals they meet: ridding farmers of blights, calming storms, summoning rains, tending the sick, settling disputes and defending the weak. They prefer reason, kindness and compromise, but will fight to protect themselves and others, and seldom fight to the death.

## GM Notes

Half the druids keep a regular circuit in one region; others wander the world spreading the ways of peace and looking for other Millennium Trees. One of their purposes is to find, buy or capture corrupted magic wands and staves and return them to the Tree of Life, and to retrieve any wand or staff used for evil, which often leads them into danger. Traditional garb is a green, tan, brown or white hooded robe or cloak, bark or leaf armor and sandals of wood or cloth. A druid can use modern weapons and machines but few have any at the start; magic items count as natural.
